entries[1224877] = { ["name"] = "Lightfused Herbs", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nA strange light has begun to afflict the herbs growing within Quel'Thalas. They grow large and golden, reminiscent of the Sunwell itself, but twisted somehow. Gathering these herbs will release motes of holy energy that sear if caught, but yield additional resources." }
entries[1224878] = { ["name"] = "Primal Herbs", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nHarandar is a land thrumming with primordial magic. Deep down within Azeroth, this magic has stewed and coalesced for eons, and the local flora has grown stronger for it.\n\nUpon gathering these primal herbs, they gift you with some of their energy in the form of an additional charge for your Skyriding abilities." }
entries[1224879] = { ["name"] = "Wild Herbs", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nZul'Aman -- a land rife with natural magic and ancient power. This power permeates all things in Zul'Aman, and has come to affect the herbs found within the region.\n\nGathering these wild herbs releases a burst of nature magic, giving rise to a group of hostile herb lashers that attempt to take vengeance!" }
entries[1224880] = { ["name"] = "Void Herbs", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nWhile the power of the void has been present on Azeroth since time immemorial, recent events have caused it to surge. It has managed to seep into the world, which has had adverse affects on the local ecology.\n\nIn some cases, the unstable energies of the void have caused these herbs to be sent across the Twisting Nether to parts unknown. In this case, you happened to find this specimen in the Voidstorm." }
entries[1224881] = { ["name"] = "Emote State - Dance" }
entries[1224882] = { ["name"] = "Lightfused Argentleaf", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nThe silverleaf of Quel'Thalas has grown more lustrous in recent years, gaining a unique sheen that allows anyone to recognize it at a glance. Because of these changes, this new offshoot of silverleaf has become known as argentleaf.\n\nRegularly found among other common foliage, it is a standard ingredient of many recipes and is thus highly sought after.\n\nA strange light has begun to afflict the herbs growing within Quel'Thalas. They grow large and golden, reminiscent of the Sunwell itself, but twisted somehow. Gathering these herbs will release motes of holy energy that sear if caught, but yield additional resources.\nDiscovery:\nMidnight Gathering Nodes" }
entries[1224883] = { ["name"] = "Lightfused Tranquility Bloom", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nThe environmental factors and changes of Quel'Thalas and the surrounding regions has had a profound impact on the local flora, including even the humble Peacebloom. It is still a staple of local crafting and is utilized in a wide variety of recipes, and a recent strain that has adapted to those changes has been dubbed Tranquility Bloom.\n\nA strange light has begun to afflict the herbs growing within Quel'Thalas. They grow large and golden, reminiscent of the Sunwell itself, but twisted somehow. Gathering these herbs will release motes of holy energy that sear if caught, but yield additional resources.\nDiscovery:\nMidnight Gathering Nodes" }
entries[1224884] = { ["name"] = "Lightfused Mana Lily", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nAnother recent offshoot species, mana lily is a new variant of mageroyal. The latent magic present in the Quel'Thalas region has seeped into the mana lily, giving them potent properties for crafting.\n\nIf you're ever gathering around bodies of water, you can expect to find mana lilies somewhere nearby.\n\nA strange light has begun to afflict the herbs growing within Quel'Thalas. They grow large and golden, reminiscent of the Sunwell itself, but twisted somehow. Gathering these herbs will release motes of holy energy that sear if caught, but yield additional resources.\nDiscovery:\nMidnight Gathering Nodes" }
entries[1224885] = { ["name"] = "Lightfused Azeroot", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nThe hearty earthroot plant has grown stronger in recent years. Difficult to gather, but just as potent in crafting, azeroot is key to many recipes in Quel'Thalas.\n\nThis sturdy wooden herb can be found on or around trees in the Quel'Thalas region.\n\nA strange light has begun to afflict the herbs growing within Quel'Thalas. They grow large and golden, reminiscent of the Sunwell itself, but twisted somehow. Gathering these herbs will release motes of holy energy that sear if caught, but yield additional resources.\nDiscovery:\nMidnight Gathering Nodes" }
entries[1224886] = { ["name"] = "Lightfused Sanguithorn", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nOnce only usable as an edible plant for fleeting magical power, recent evolutionary changes and alchemical breakthroughs with bloodthistle have led to its use across the professions. This more potent growth has come to be known as sanguithorn, and still boasts fearsome magical capabilities.\n\nSanguithorn are known to tether themselves to rocks, either above or under the ground, so check for them in more rugged terrain.\n\nA strange light has begun to afflict the herbs growing within Quel'Thalas. They grow large and golden, reminiscent of the Sunwell itself, but twisted somehow. Gathering these herbs will release motes of holy energy that sear if caught, but yield additional resources.\nDiscovery:\nMidnight Gathering Nodes" }
entries[1224887] = { ["name"] = "Primal Argentleaf", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nThe silverleaf of Quel'Thalas has grown more lustrous in recent years, gaining a unique sheen that allows anyone to recognize it at a glance. Because of these changes, this new offshoot of silverleaf has become known as argentleaf.\n\nRegularly found among other common foliage, it is a standard ingredient of many recipes and is thus highly sought after.\n\nHarandar is a land thrumming with primordial magic. Deep down within Azeroth, this magic has stewed and coalesced for eons, and the local flora has grown stronger for it.\n\nUpon gathering these primal herbs, they gift you with some of their energy in the form of an additional charge for your Skyriding abilities.\nDiscovery:\nMidnight Gathering Nodes" }
entries[1224888] = { ["name"] = "Primal Tranquility Bloom", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nThe environmental factors and changes of Quel'Thalas and the surrounding regions has had a profound impact on the local flora, including even the humble Peacebloom. It is still a staple of local crafting and is utilized in a wide variety of recipes, and a recent strain that has adapted to those changes has been dubbed Tranquility Bloom.\n\nHarandar is a land thrumming with primordial magic. Deep down within Azeroth, this magic has stewed and coalesced for eons, and the local flora has grown stronger for it.\n\nUpon gathering these primal herbs, they gift you with some of their energy in the form of an additional charge for your Skyriding abilities.\nDiscovery:\nMidnight Gathering Nodes" }
entries[1224889] = { ["name"] = "Primal Mana Lily", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nAnother recent offshoot species, mana lily is a new variant of mageroyal. The latent magic present in the Quel'Thalas region has seeped into the mana lily, giving them potent properties for crafting.\n\nIf you're ever gathering around bodies of water, you can expect to find mana lilies somewhere nearby.\n\nHarandar is a land thrumming with primordial magic. Deep down within Azeroth, this magic has stewed and coalesced for eons, and the local flora has grown stronger for it.\n\nUpon gathering these primal herbs, they gift you with some of their energy in the form of an additional charge for your Skyriding abilities.\nDiscovery:\nMidnight Gathering Nodes" }
entries[1224890] = { ["name"] = "Primal Azeroot", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nThe hearty earthroot plant has grown stronger in recent years. Difficult to gather, but just as potent in crafting, azeroot is key to many recipes in Quel'Thalas.\n\nThis sturdy wooden herb can be found on or around trees in the Quel'Thalas region.\n\nHarandar is a land thrumming with primordial magic. Deep down within Azeroth, this magic has stewed and coalesced for eons, and the local flora has grown stronger for it.\n\nUpon gathering these primal herbs, they gift you with some of their energy in the form of an additional charge for your Skyriding abilities.\nDiscovery:\nMidnight Gathering Nodes" }
entries[1224891] = { ["name"] = "Primal Sanguithorn", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nOnce only usable as an edible plant for fleeting magical power, recent evolutionary changes and alchemical breakthroughs with bloodthistle have led to its use across the professions. This more potent growth has come to be known as sanguithorn, and still boasts fearsome magical capabilities.\n\nSanguithorn are known to tether themselves to rocks, either above or under the ground, so check for them in more rugged terrain.\n\nHarandar is a land thrumming with primordial magic. Deep down within Azeroth, this magic has stewed and coalesced for eons, and the local flora has grown stronger for it.\n\nUpon gathering these primal herbs, they gift you with some of their energy in the form of an additional charge for your Skyriding abilities.\nDiscovery:\nMidnight Gathering Nodes" }
entries[1224892] = { ["name"] = "Wild Argentleaf", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nThe silverleaf of Quel'Thalas has grown more lustrous in recent years, gaining a unique sheen that allows anyone to recognize it at a glance. Because of these changes, this new offshoot of silverleaf has become known as argentleaf.\n\nRegularly found among other common foliage, it is a standard ingredient of many recipes and is thus highly sought after.\n\nZul'Aman -- a land rife with natural magic and ancient power. This power permeates all things in Zul'Aman, and has come to affect the herbs found within the region.\n\nGathering these wild herbs releases a burst of nature magic, giving rise to a group of hostile herb lashers that attempt to take vengeance!\nDiscovery:\nMidnight Gathering Nodes" }
entries[1224893] = { ["name"] = "Wild Tranquility Bloom", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nThe environmental factors and changes of Quel'Thalas and the surrounding regions has had a profound impact on the local flora, including even the humble Peacebloom. It is still a staple of local crafting and is utilized in a wide variety of recipes, and a recent strain that has adapted to those changes has been dubbed Tranquility Bloom.\n\nZul'Aman -- a land rife with natural magic and ancient power. This power permeates all things in Zul'Aman, and has come to affect the herbs found within the region.\n\nGathering these wild herbs releases a burst of nature magic, giving rise to a group of hostile herb lashers that attempt to take vengeance!\nDiscovery:\nMidnight Gathering Nodes" }
